CODE EXPLAINED
1. Import libraries
python
import requests
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
requests: Downloads the website webpage.
BeautifulSoup: Parses HTML and extracts information from the webpage.

2. Website URL
python
url = "https://books.toscrape.com/"
Stores the website address from which we want to extract product information.

3. Fetch and parse webpage
python
soup = BeautifulSoup(requests.get(url).text, "html.parser")
requests.get(url) sends a request to the website.
.text retrieves the webpage HTML content.
BeautifulSoup() converts HTML into a searchable structure.
html.parser parses the HTML content.

4. Extract product information
python
for product in soup.select(".product_pod"):
Selects all product containers from the webpage.
.product_pod is a CSS selector.
Each product container represents one book.

5. Extract product name
python
name = product.h3.a["title"]
Extracts the book name from the title attribute.

6. Extract product price
python
price = product.select_one(".price_color").text
select_one() selects the first matching HTML element.
.price_color identifies the price.
.text extracts the price as text.

7. Extract product link
python
link = "https://books.toscrape.com/catalogue/" + product.h3.a["href"]
Extracts the product webpage link.
["href"] gets the link address.
+ joins the website address with the product link to create a complete URL.

